1. CRITICAL: DUPLICATE HERO SECTION CSS (DRY VIOLATION)
================================================================================

The exact same `.hero-para-wrapper` / `.hero-para` block is duplicated across 
12 page components with minor variations:

Pattern A (`.hero-para-wrapper` with `border-left` + `margin: 2rem 0`):
  - components/trends/trends.css:24-28
  - components/trend-details/trend-details.css:24-28
  - components/trend-and-cases/case-studies.css:24-28
  - components/services/service.css:57-61
  - components/organization/org.css:32-36
  - components/opportunities/opportunities.css:32-36
  - components/job-seekers/job-seekers.css:32-36
  - components/contact-us/contact-us.css:32-36
  - components/case-study-details/case-study-detail.css:35-39
  - components/case-studies/all-case-studies.css:24-28
  - components/candidates/candidates.css:32-36

Pattern B (`.hero-para` with `border-left` + `margin` with responsive values):
  - components/about/about.css:52-65 (uses single `margin: 2rem 0`, no MQ for margin)
  - components/landing/landing.css:108-143 (uses granular MQs: margin varies per breakpoint)

Pattern C (`.hero-para-wrapper` with `border-left` + `margin: 2rem 0` with extra `.hero-para` inside):
  - This is the most common — 11 identical copies

FIX: Create a shared `.hero-para-wrapper` class in globals.css and remove from 
page-level CSS. Each component only needs to override if different.

