2. CRITICAL: TWO DIFFERENT BREAKPOINT SYSTEMS
================================================================================

System A (Granular — 5 breakpoints) — used in:
  globals.css, landing.css, footer.css, header.css, slider.css, 
  vertical-slider.css, golden-section.css, section-frame.css, 
  feat-card.css, candidate-card.css, button-action.css
  Breakpoints: 480px, 767px, 1023px, 1279px, 1536px, 1920px

System B (Simplified — 1-2 breakpoints) — used in:
  trends.css, trend-details.css, case-studies.css, service.css, 
  org.css, opportunities.css, job-seekers.css, contact-us.css, 
  case-study-detail.css, all-case-studies.css, candidates.css, 
  about.css, cookie-policy.css, input-field.css, tag-ui.css
  Breakpoints: 600px, 767px, 768px, 1024px, 1025px

PROBLEM: System A uses the granular approach with specific ranges like 
"481-767px" and "768-1023px". System B uses a simpler "max-width: 767px" 
approach. This creates gaps — e.g., at 600px some System B components 
switch layout while System A components don't.

RECOMMENDATION: Standardize on ONE breakpoint system across the entire 
project. System A is more thorough but adds complexity. System B is simpler 
but misses edge cases. Pick one and migrate.

